From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: no rx URB in flight after the bus stop

From code reading (pinned tag plus the earlier patches of this series; kernel 6.18.53).

aicwf_usb_bus_stop() (as changed by aic_load_fw-no-rx-refill-after-the-bus-has-stopped) cancels a pending refill, sets USB_DOWN_ST
and kills the anchored rx URBs (aicwf_usb.c:767-770 after aic8800-init-the-rx-refill-work-before-the-first-error-path). A
completion that lands between the cancel and the state change still sees
USB_UP_ST and queues a refill (:231-237, :280). That refill can pass both
state checks (:336, :296) before the state change, sleep in
__dev_alloc_skb(GFP_KERNEL) (:302) while the stop kills the anchor, and
anchor and submit afterwards (:317, :319). On the disconnect path no URB
completes there (see the header of that patch). On the probe's error path (a failed
configuration or upload, :1892, :1896) the part is still on the bus,
out_free frees usb_dev with that URB in flight (:1913), and its completion
runs on freed memory.

In the vendor driver: the stop kills the rx URBs once and assumes no
one submits afterwards, but the refill work checks the state and submits
without anything that orders the two against the stop.

What changes: after the kill, the stop cancels the work once more, which
waits for a refill that is still running, and kills the anchor once more.
After the state change nothing queues a refill (every completion sees
USB_DOWN_ST), and usb_kill_anchored_urbs() returns only when no
completion of an anchored URB is running: the core counts
suspend_wakeups around ->complete() (drivers/usb/core/hcd.c:1648-1664) and
the kill waits for that count (drivers/usb/core/urb.c:813-836). So after
the second kill no rx URB is in flight and no refill is pending. The
refill that straddles the change still prints "usb state is not up!" and
"usb rx refill fail" for its next buffer; that is the state it finds.

Not taken:
- The second cancel alone: the refill it waits for may already have
  submitted.
- The state change before the first cancel, which would make the second
  pass unnecessary for a refill that has not started: the earlier patch put the cancel
  first so that a pending refill does not run and print; that reason
  stands.
- A lock over check and submit: the submit path sleeps (GFP_KERNEL, and
  msleep(100) after a failed submit, :326).

Test stimulus and counters under /sys/module/aic_load_fw/parameters:
rx_loader_inject_stop_race (0644): the next N probes take the error path of
a failed configuration right after the bus start, with the part on the bus
and its rx URBs live. Their stop kills one rx URB while the bus is up, so
that its completion queues the refill, holds that refill after both state
checks, lets it go once the stop has killed the anchor, and then counts
rx_loader_urb_after_stop (0444) if an rx URB is still in flight -- and kills
it, so the stimulus itself never frees usb_dev under a live URB.
rx_loader_stop_race_missed (0444) counts runs whose refill never reached the
hold point.

Falsifier, on the board, with the part at its loaded id:
  modprobe -r aic8800_fdrv aic_load_fw
  modprobe aic_load_fw rx_loader_inject_stop_race=1
Without the fix: rx_loader_urb_after_stop 1 per run; with it: 0, and
rx_loader_stop_race_missed 0. One count with the fix refutes it.

HW-proven, 8 GiB board, 2026-09-24 (6.18.53): three runs each; the stimulus
alone left an rx URB in flight after the stop every time, with this patch
none, and the refill held on every run of both.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
index ca98bb3..3899334 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -220,6 +220,35 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_refill_skipped, "rx completions on a stopped bus that
 static int rx_loader_inject_pending_refill;
 module_param(rx_loader_inject_pending_refill, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_inject_pending_refill, "Test stimulus: the next N disconnects queue the rx refill before they stop the bus");
+static int rx_loader_inject_stop_race;
+module_param(rx_loader_inject_stop_race, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_inject_stop_race, "Test stimulus: the next N probes take the error path after the bus start, and their bus stop holds one rx refill between its state checks and its submit until the rx URBs are killed");
+static uint rx_loader_urb_after_stop;
+module_param(rx_loader_urb_after_stop, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_urb_after_stop, "stimulus runs that found an rx URB in flight after the bus stop (the stimulus kills it then)");
+static uint rx_loader_stop_race_missed;
+module_param(rx_loader_stop_race_missed, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_stop_race_missed, "stimulus runs whose refill never reached the hold point");
+
+/* rx_loader_inject_stop_race: one refill that has found the bus up is held
+ * before it submits and let go once the stop has killed the rx URBs -- the
+ * window a refill opens that sleeps in its skb allocation while the bus
+ * stops. One device at a time; a test stimulus, not a mechanism.
+ */
+static bool stop_race_pending;
+static bool stop_race_armed;
+static bool stop_race_holding;
+static DECLARE_COMPLETION(stop_race_held);
+static DECLARE_COMPLETION(stop_race_go);
+static DECLARE_COMPLETION(stop_race_done);
+
+static void aicwf_usb_stop_race_submitted(void)
+{
+    if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(stop_race_holding))) {
+        WRITE_ONCE(stop_race_holding, false);
+        complete(&stop_race_done);
+    }
+}
 
 /* No refill work may run once the bus is down: it would only find
  * USB_DOWN_ST in aicwf_usb_rx_submit_all_urb() and report it as an error.
@@ -299,6 +328,13 @@ static int aicwf_usb_submit_rx_urb(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev,
         return -1;
     }
 
+    if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(stop_race_armed))) {
+        WRITE_ONCE(stop_race_armed, false);
+        WRITE_ONCE(stop_race_holding, true);
+        complete(&stop_race_held);
+        wait_for_completion_timeout(&stop_race_go, msecs_to_jiffies(2000));
+    }
+
     skb = __dev_alloc_skb(AICWF_USB_MAX_PKT_SIZE, GFP_KERNEL);
     if (!skb) {
         aicwf_usb_rx_buf_put(usb_dev, usb_buf);
@@ -343,7 +379,10 @@ static void aicwf_usb_rx_submit_all_urb(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev)
 }
 
     while((usb_buf = aicwf_usb_rx_buf_get(usb_dev)) != NULL) {
-        if (aicwf_usb_submit_rx_urb(usb_dev, usb_buf)) {
+        int err = aicwf_usb_submit_rx_urb(usb_dev, usb_buf);
+
+        aicwf_usb_stop_race_submitted();
+        if (err) {
             usb_err("usb rx refill fail\n");
             if (usb_dev->state != USB_UP_ST){
                 return;
@@ -752,10 +791,56 @@ static void aicwf_usb_cancel_all_urbs(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev)
     usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&usb_dev->rx_submitted);
 }
 
+/* Stimulus, before USB_DOWN_ST: kill one rx URB on the live bus, so that its
+ * completion queues the refill, and wait until that refill holds.
+ */
+static bool aicwf_usb_stop_race_hold(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev)
+{
+    struct urb *urb;
+
+    if (likely(!stop_race_pending) || usb_dev->state != USB_UP_ST)
+        return false;
+    stop_race_pending = false;
+    reinit_completion(&stop_race_held);
+    reinit_completion(&stop_race_go);
+    reinit_completion(&stop_race_done);
+    WRITE_ONCE(stop_race_armed, true);
+    urb = usb_get_from_anchor(&usb_dev->rx_submitted);
+    if (urb) {
+        usb_kill_urb(urb);
+        usb_put_urb(urb);
+    }
+    if (!urb || !wait_for_completion_timeout(&stop_race_held, msecs_to_jiffies(2000))) {
+        WRITE_ONCE(stop_race_armed, false);
+        rx_loader_stop_race_missed++;
+        pr_warn("aic_load_fw: stop race stimulus: no refill reached the hold point\n");
+        return false;
+    }
+    pr_info("aic_load_fw: stop race stimulus: refill held past its state checks\n");
+    return true;
+}
+
+/* Stimulus, at the end of the stop: count an rx URB that is still in flight,
+ * then kill it, so the run does not free usb_dev under it.
+ */
+static void aicwf_usb_stop_race_check(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev)
+{
+    if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&stop_race_done, msecs_to_jiffies(2000)))
+        pr_warn("aic_load_fw: stop race stimulus: the held refill did not submit\n");
+    if (!usb_anchor_empty(&usb_dev->rx_submitted)) {
+        rx_loader_urb_after_stop++;
+        pr_warn("aic_load_fw: stop race stimulus: rx URB in flight after the bus stop, killed now\n");
+        usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&usb_dev->rx_submitted);
+    } else {
+        pr_info("aic_load_fw: stop race stimulus: no rx URB in flight after the bus stop\n");
+    }
+}
+
 static void aicwf_usb_bus_stop(struct device *dev)
 {
     struct aicwf_bus *bus_if = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
     struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev = bus_if->bus_priv.usb;
+    bool race;
 
     if (usb_dev == NULL)
         return;
@@ -766,8 +851,20 @@ static void aicwf_usb_bus_stop(struct device *dev)
     /* Before USB_DOWN_ST, see aicwf_usb_rx_refill(). */
     if (cancel_work_sync(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work))
         rx_loader_refill_cancelled++;
+    race = aicwf_usb_stop_race_hold(usb_dev);
     aicwf_usb_state_change(usb_dev, USB_DOWN_ST);
     aicwf_usb_cancel_all_urbs(usb_dev);
+    if (race)
+        complete(&stop_race_go);
+    /* A refill that found the bus up before the state change can still
+     * submit after the kill above: wait for it, then kill what it
+     * sent. Nothing queues a refill any more -- every completion now sees
+     * USB_DOWN_ST -- so after this no rx URB is in flight.
+     */
+    cancel_work_sync(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work);
+    usb_kill_anchored_urbs(&usb_dev->rx_submitted);
+    if (race)
+        aicwf_usb_stop_race_check(usb_dev);
 }
 
 static void aicwf_usb_deinit(struct aic_usb_dev *usbdev)
@@ -1874,6 +1971,16 @@ static int aicwf_usb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf, const struct usb_device_i
 
     aic_bt_platform_init(usb_dev);
 
+    /* Stimulus: the error path of a failed configuration (system_config()
+     * below), taken with the part still on the bus and its rx URBs live.
+     */
+    if (unlikely(rx_loader_inject_stop_race > 0)) {
+        rx_loader_inject_stop_race--;
+        stop_race_pending = true;
+        usb_err("stop race stimulus: error path after the bus start\n");
+        goto out_free_bus;
+    }
+
     if ((usb->speed != USB_SPEED_HIGH) && (usb->speed != USB_SPEED_SUPER)) {
         printk("Aic USB device detected speed = %d\n", usb->speed);
         system_reboot(usb_dev);
